ll so now when you take those guys and  you put them with our running backs mark  ingram who we signed this year just  edwards kenneth dixon  justice hill who we drafted we feel like  we've got a really intriguing set of  play makers to help lamar move the ball  effectively  let me flip it over to december  defensive side of the ball you had  several guys leave via free agency eric  weddle was cut you know fans get nervous  when they see these recognizable names  leaving the team  what do you say to the folks who think  the defense is going to take a step back  because so many names people are  familiar with aren't going to be there  anymore  well i mean i understand their concern  and we're concerned about that as well  but we've been through this before we've  had  multiple times over the last however  many years 20 years i'd say where we've  had these sort of purges where we've  lost veteran players it happened in 2002  it happened in 2007. it's happened it  happened the year that we traded hello  to nada away  you know so it happened when we lost ray  lewis we lost ed reed  it's happened many times in baltimore  and the one constant is we've been able  to rebuild the defense pretty quickly  and stay strong and so in looking at our  defense i think we've got a really  really wonderful secondary a very  talented secondary with some outstanding  players i love our defensive line up  front we got michael pierce and brandon  williams two guys that can really play  the run and play stout in there we've  got some really good i think young  ascending linebackers and peanut and  warsaw and kenny young who we drafted  last year matt judon who we think is one  of the more intriguing outside  linebackers in football with his skill  set as a pass rusher and a young  outside player who can make plays  so the coverage not bare we had to make  some really tough decisions salary cap  related we knew the market would be  irrational in one sense  and we saw zadarius smith and t.j 