lk about other positions there's been  comparisons to julian edelman is he a  quarterback and only a quarterback with  the ravens or could he play other  positions  that's a great question i think he's a  football player and everything that that  entails i think his skill set is buried  in multiple we brought him in we spent a  day with him here in baltimore several  weeks ago  we worked him out as a quarterback  but this is a guy that he's fast he's  strong he's tough he's a playmaker he's  a football player and we've seen teams  for instance the new orleans saints at  pace and hell we've seen other teams  find ways to play with players like this  and they can help you win football games  so he fits our defense  fits our offense he fits special teams  he's got a great mentality he's a leader  he's highly competitive he's played in a  lot of big games and we're excited to  see what he can do  did you miss speak or did you intend to  say he fits our defense  i think he fits everything this guy's a  football player he pulls the ball away  he runs the ball well he's been a safety  he could probably return kicks he could  probably punt if we need him to punt  he's a talented kid he's super smart  he's highly competitive and uh we just  want to find his niche we're going to  carve out a niche for him  he gives us a lot of possibilities we  played against the saints this year we  got a chance to see what tayson hill  could do  first hand and uh when you got a guy  like that you can line up at quarterback  you can run with him he can throw the  football  he plays on the special teams as a  personal protector you can fake kicks  with them that's a weapon we're going to  try to use our guy the same way  well eric you you found your niche 23  years ago here's to 23 more  congratulations on all your success we  look forward to talking again soon  thanks mike i appreciate it  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

